# Credentials — never commit. Alpaca keys: ALPACA_<BOOK>_KEY_ID / _SECRET_KEY.
config/.env
config/.env.*
.env

# Market data (gigabytes). Rebuilt by the fetchers in scripts/cef/.
# LEADING SLASH IS LOAD-BEARING: a bare `data/` would also match any src/**/data/.
/data/

# An analyst's private Python for this repo (docs/ONBOARDING.md §2.2).
/.venv/

# Caches and scratch
**/__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
results/**/_cache_*
# The live attribution's cache (scripts/cef/live_attribution.py fetch): the cef
# paper account's FILL activities and EOD equity series. This repository is
# public; account fills are never committed (docs/REFERENCES.md §12an keeps the
# series of record outside the repository for the same reason).
results/cef/live_attribution/_cache/
# Its analyse outputs carry the same account data (daily.csv holds the EOD equity
# of every session); the tool refuses to write either where git can see it.
results/cef/live_attribution/_out/
results/cef/live_attribution/_out_c4/
# The evidence pack's row-level live records (per name, per fill, positions). Team lead,
# 2026-11-03: "Aggregates in repo, rows private". results/**/_cache_* covers it too; this line
# says so by name, and scripts/report/tests pins it.
results/report/_cache_live/
.ipynb_checkpoints/
*.log

# macOS
.DS_Store

# Runtime halt/heartbeat records (ops/halt.py). Written inside the prod clone at
# run time; untracked so a (cleared) halt never blocks the installer's clean-tree
# check. The runner reads the halt at run time, so ignoring it here cannot let a
# standing halt be skipped.
/ops/HALT*.md
/ops/halts/
/ops/heartbeat.json

# Background agents' git worktrees (Claude Code); second copies of the repo.
/.claude/worktrees/

# Row-level tables derived from licensed WRDS data (CRSP, TRACE): permnos, CUSIPs,
# delisting records and per-event returns. This repository is public, so they stay
# on disk only; the scripts named in results/events/REPRO_*_2026-10-11.md rebuild
# them. Aggregates (*_summary.json, run logs, per-fund beta tables) are tracked.
results/events/merger_events_2010_2022.csv
results/events/merger_pairs_fixed_offset.csv
results/events/merger_acquirers_2010_2022.csv
results/events/merger_ann_sample.csv
results/events/alpaca_acquirers_2026-10-11.csv
results/events/term_pull_to_par_measure.csv
# Since 2026-10-22 their writers write into a project folder (acquirer_shortability.py
# -> g1a/, term_pull_to_par.py -> term_cef/). The two lines above stay: copies
# already on disk at the old paths must remain ignored.
results/events/g1a/alpaca_acquirers_2026-10-11.csv
results/events/term_cef/term_pull_to_par_measure.csv
results/events/term_cef_census.csv
results/events/convert_issuance_events.csv
# EDGAR-dated merger tables (2026-10-12) join CRSP rows (permnos, CRSP names and
# tickers, per-event returns): on disk only, like the rows above. The summaries
# (merger_edgar_dates_summary.json, merger_ann_edgar_summary.json) are tracked.
results/events/merger_edgar_dates.csv
results/events/merger_ann_sample_edgar.csv
results/events/g6_events_13_names.csv
# g6_corporate_action_shorts.py writes into g6/ since 2026-10-22; the line above
# stays for a copy already on disk at the old path.
results/events/g6/g6_events_13_names.csv

# EDGAR (public, but large and re-fetchable): the response cache is
# results/events/_cache_edgar/ (already covered by results/**/_cache_*); the
# full filings table (~88k rows) is rebuilt from it by
# `scripts/data/fetch_edgar_events.py --offline`. Its episodes table and
# summary are tracked.
results/events/edgar_cef_bdc_filings.csv.gz
# Gate G1a (2026-10-13, scripts/events/g1a_shortability.py): the per-deal table
# and the row-level detail carry CRSP names and permnos (licensed); the tracked
# outputs are g1a_summary_<date>.json (counts) and g1a_pending_<date>.csv
# (EDGAR, Alpaca and IBKR only).
results/events/g1a_historical_deals.csv
results/events/g1a_detail_*.json
# g1a_shortability.py writes into g1a/ since 2026-10-22; the two lines above stay
# for copies already on disk at the old paths.
results/events/g1a/g1a_historical_deals.csv
results/events/g1a/g1a_detail_*.json
# E1 ETF-hedge gate (2026-10-15, scripts/events/e1_etf_hedge_gate.py): the
# per-target x hedge table carries CRSP permnos and statistics computed on CRSP
# returns (licensed); the tracked output is e1_etf_hedge_summary_<date>.json
# (segment aggregates, Alpaca and IBKR rows).
results/events/e1_etf_hedge_detail.csv

# Conditional-tender census (2026-10-13): the full table carries window averages
# computed on CRSP closes (licensed); the tracked conditional_tender_census.csv
# blanks them. Rebuilt by scripts/events/conditional_tender_census.py.
results/events/conditional_tender_census_full.csv

# CEF corporate-action census (2026-10-15, scripts/events/cef_corp_action_census.py):
# the full per-event table joins CRSP (permnos, closes, ADV, discounts); the
# tracked cef_corp_action_events.csv carries EDGAR facts only, and the per-type
# cef_corp_action_census.csv and the summary JSON are aggregates.
results/events/cef_corp_action_events_full.csv

# Trial P&L series (scripts/research/registry.py): the repo is public and an event
# book's series can be a licensed security's return. The tracked ledger holds each
# series' sha256.
/results/research/trials/series/

# Exposure readout (scripts/cef/exposure_readout.py, 2026-11-02, report only): the keyless
# yfinance cache, and the analyse outputs, which carry the caller's positions and equity.
# This repository is public; the module also refuses any path git can see.
results/cef/exposure_readout/_cache/
results/cef/exposure_readout/_out/
results/cef/exposure_readout/_out_c4/
